  "conduct": "The user comes back to close the payments discussion out. Shown that E1 was put down and why, they take it in stride: with the sandbox no longer mirroring production delivery timing there is nothing left to measure, and they would rather settle the window by judgment than wait for a rebuilt sandbox. They decide it themselves — a three-second wait before the checkout surfaces the pending state, revisited if support complaints arrive — and they want no successor experiment. When the point is written up they say that covers it and ask to wrap up. On the way out they are agreeable to required steps — a mandatory review pass or the conclusion gets a yes — and they decline optional extras: no new threads, no second look. They introduce no new material.",
